title: Lost in Committee
subtitle: The bureaucrats are slow-walking our bills.
tags: event
view-if: bureau_relation < 25 and (rc_in_govt or rc_chairs > 0) and not bureau_warn_cold and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 2
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_chancellery.svg
on-arrival: bureau_warn_cold = 1

= Lost in Committee

Caucus amendments have started to go missing. Hearings are postponed for "scheduling reasons". Briefing papers arrive the morning after the vote. The Senate bureaucracy has turned **cold** towards the Caucus.

They dislike the company we keep in government and the reforms we have pushed through. Until relations improve, **our reform bills lose support in committee** (3 points off every vote we sponsor). If they turn hostile, they will try to force us out.

*Ways to win them back: Finis Valorum, Bail Organa or Bail Antilles can work with the bureaucrats as advisors; the Judiciary & Intelligence Committee can reform the bureaucracy; a more establishment coalition, or easing off the guilds, reassures them.*

- @soothe: Make concessions to the committee staff.
- @expose: Expose the obstruction publicly.
- @carry_on: Carry on regardless.

@soothe
subtitle: −1 political capital; the bureaucrats are mollified for now.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; bureau_relation += 10

New office space, a few promotions, a quiet word that the Caucus is "not unreasonable". The missing amendments reappear.

@expose
subtitle: The Senate takes note; the bureaucrats take it personally.
on-arrival: senate_resolve += 0.5; faith += 0.5; bureau_relation -= 5

The HoloNet runs the story of the amendments that vanished. The Senate is briefly outraged. The bureaucracy is not briefly anything.

@carry_on

The Caucus will not be bullied by clerks. The clerks make a note of it.
